### Test Forgot Password & Reset Password Flow
### Proper 2-Step Flow with Email Verification

@baseUrl = http://localhost:3001
@email = test@example.com
@resetToken = PASTE_TOKEN_FROM_EMAIL_HERE
@newPassword = newpassword123

###############################################
### STEP 1: Forgot Password (Request Reset)
###############################################

### 1. Request password reset
### User hanya input email
### Sistem akan generate token dan kirim ke email
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/forgot-password
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{email}}"
}

### Response:
### {
###   "message": "Jika email terdaftar, link reset password akan dikirim ke email Anda."
### }

### 2. Check email
### User akan menerima email dengan link:
### http://localhost:3000/auth/reset-password?token=abc123xyz...
###
### Copy token dari email dan paste ke variable @resetToken di atas

###############################################
### STEP 2: Reset Password (Set New Password)
###############################################

### 3. Reset password dengan token dari email
### User input password baru saja, token sudah dari URL
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/reset-password
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "token": "{{resetToken}}",
  "password": "{{newPassword}}"
}

### Response:
### {
###   "message": "Password berhasil direset. Silakan login dengan password baru Anda."
### }

###############################################
### STEP 3: Login dengan Password Baru
###############################################

### 4. Test login dengan password baru
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{email}}",
  "password": "{{newPassword}}"
}

### Response: Should return accessToken, refreshToken, sessionId

###############################################
### Error Cases
###############################################

### 5. Test dengan token invalid
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/reset-password
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "token": "invalid-token-12345",
  "password": "newpassword123"
}

### Response: 
### {
###   "statusCode": 401,
###   "message": "Invalid or expired reset token"
### }

### 6. Test dengan token expired
### (Token otomatis expired setelah 1 jam)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/reset-password
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "token": "expired-token-from-1-hour-ago",
  "password": "newpassword123"
}

### Response:
### {
###   "statusCode": 401,
###   "message": "Reset token has expired"
### }

### 7. Test dengan token yang sudah digunakan
### (Token hanya bisa digunakan 1x)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/reset-password
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "token": "already-used-token",
  "password": "newpassword123"
}

### Response:
### {
###   "statusCode": 401,
###   "message": "Reset token already used"
### }

### 8. Request reset untuk email yang tidak terdaftar
### (Response tetap sama untuk security)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/forgot-password
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "nonexistent@example.com"
}

### Response:
### {
###   "message": "Jika email terdaftar, link reset password akan dikirim ke email Anda."
### }
### Note: Email TIDAK akan dikirim, tapi response tetap sama

###############################################
### Legacy Endpoint (INSECURE - Deprecated)
###############################################

### 9. Legacy reset password tanpa token (TIDAK AMAN!)
### ⚠️ WARNING: Deprecated endpoint, akan dihapus!
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/reset-password-legacy
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{email}}",
  "password": "hackme123"
}

### Response:
### {
###   "message": "Password reset successful"
### }
### ❌ Ini TIDAK AMAN karena tidak ada verification!

###############################################
### Complete Testing Flow
###############################################

### Step-by-step testing:

# 1. Register user baru (jika belum ada)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Test User",
  "email": "testforgot@example.com",
  "password": "oldpassword123"
}

# 2. Verify email terlebih dahulu
# (Check email dan klik verification link)

# 3. Login dengan password lama
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "testforgot@example.com",
  "password": "oldpassword123"
}

# 4. Request forgot password
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/forgot-password
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "testforgot@example.com"
}

# 5. Check email, copy token dari URL
# URL format: http://localhost:3000/auth/reset-password?token=abc123...

# 6. Reset password dengan token
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/reset-password
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "token": "PASTE_TOKEN_HERE",
  "password": "newpassword123"
}

# 7. Test login dengan password baru
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "testforgot@example.com",
  "password": "newpassword123"
}

# 8. Verify: Login dengan password lama harus gagal
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "testforgot@example.com",
  "password": "oldpassword123"
}

### Response: Should return 401 Unauthorized

###############################################
### Database Checks (Optional)
###############################################

### Check password reset tokens in database:
### 
### SELECT * FROM sys_PasswordReset WHERE user_id = {user_id};
###
### Columns:
### - id: Auto increment ID
### - user_id: User ID
### - token: Hashed token (64 characters hex)
### - expiresAt: Expiration time (1 hour from created)
### - createdAt: When token was created
### - used: Boolean (false = not used, true = already used)

### Check if all sessions revoked after password reset:
###
### SELECT * FROM sys_Session WHERE user_id = {user_id} AND isActive = true;
###
### Should return empty (all sessions revoked for security)

